Square-substitution Burnside templates
  A=A000568(n); template = sum_[base B] (1/|Aut(B)|) sum_g A^cycles(g).
  This counts fiber-class assignments to base vertices, modulo base symmetry.
   n     A  A^2 uniform      raw A^(n+1)        templates  aut_order_hist
   1     1            1                1                1  {1: 1}
   2     1            1                1                1  {1: 1}
   3     2            4               16               12  {1: 1, 3: 1}
   4     4           16            1,024              704  {1: 2, 3: 2}
   5    12          144        2,985,984        2,127,984  {1: 7, 3: 4, 5: 1}

Block path-cover formula for H on lexicographic products
  H(base[fibers]) = sum_run_counts macro_words(base,r) * prod_i PathCovers(F_i,r_i).
  The naive product H(base)*prod H(fiber_i) fails once the outer base has cycles.
  chain3[chain3,chain3,chain3]       direct=1        formula=1        naive=1      ok=True
  cycle3[chain3,chain3,chain3]       direct=2721     formula=2721     naive=3      ok=True
  cycle3[cycle3,chain3,cycle3]       direct=2961     formula=2961     naive=27     ok=True
  chain3[cycle3,chain3,cycle3]       direct=9        formula=9        naive=9      ok=True

